<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Izumo Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Izumo Province was an old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan">Sea of Japan</a> coast, in the east of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimane-prefecture">Shimane Prefecture</a>. It is the setting of many myths in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kojiki">Kojiki</a> and home to the Izumo Grand Shrine, one of Japan's oldest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shinto">Shinto</a> sanctuaries. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a> it was the base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amago-clan">Amago clan</a>, and under the Tokugawa it formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matsue">Matsue</a> domain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/izumo-province.jpg" alt="Izumo Province" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Izumo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
